														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1325153">
									

<p>Well, depending on technology you could also make deliberate disobedience of authority figures &quot;psychologically impossible / literally unthinkable&quot; <em>(hello University!)</em> or just ensure that a certain social and media climate renders the dissident elements less attractive to overwhelming majority than the State-approved alternative(s) (pretty much doable today). Of course, combining that with surveillance won't hurt, but using &quot;smarter dissent management&quot; one could save a lot of resources by decreasing minimum scale of surveillance and enforcement infrastructure needed to maintain the &quot;dystopian&quot; society.</p>
<p>There are probably thousands upon thousands of ways to construct and maintain various &quot;stable dystopias&quot; (some more technologically feasible than others ;-) )</p>

							</div>

								
